<div class="about-container">
  <div class="about-header">
    <h1><svg width="30" height="30" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="#icon-info" xlink:href="#icon-info"></use></svg> About This Project</h1>
    <p>Learn about the Binary Color Generator and its educational purpose</p>
  </div>

  <div class="about-content">
    <!-- Project Overview -->
    <section class="about-section">
      <h2><svg class="section-icon" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="#icon-book" xlink:href="#icon-book"></use></svg> Project Overview</h2>
      <p>
        The <strong>Binary Color Generator</strong> is an interactive web-based
        educational tool that demonstrates the fundamental relationship between
        binary numbers and digital color representation in computer systems.
      </p>
      <p>
        This project bridges the conceptual gap between abstract binary concepts
        and concrete visual outcomes, helping students understand how computers
        represent and display colors using only 0s and 1s.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- How It Works -->
    <section class="about-section">
      <h2><svg class="section-icon" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="#icon-process" xlink:href="#icon-process"></use></svg> How It Works</h2>
      <div class="workflow">
        <div class="workflow-step">
          <div class="icon-badge">1</div>
          <div class="step-content">
            <h3>Input Binary Values</h3>
            <p>
              Enter 8-bit binary strings for Red, Green, and Blue channels
              (e.g., 11111111)
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="workflow-step">
          <div class="icon-badge">2</div>
          <div class="step-content">
            <h3>Binary to Decimal Conversion</h3>
            <p>
              Each 8-bit binary string is converted to a decimal value (0-255)
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="workflow-step">
          <div class="icon-badge">3</div>
          <div class="step-content">
            <h3>Color Generation</h3>
            <p>The three decimal values combine to create an RGB color</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="workflow-step">
          <div class="icon-badge">4</div>
          <div class="step-content">
            <h3>Visual Display</h3>
            <p>
              The color is displayed with its RGB, Hex, and 24-bit binary
              representations
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Technology Stack -->
    <section class="about-section">
      <h2><svg class="section-icon" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="#icon-tools" xlink:href="#icon-tools"></use></svg> Technology Stack</h2>
      <div class="tech-stack">
        <div class="tech-item">Node.js</div>
        <div class="tech-item">Express.js</div>
        <div class="tech-item">EJS Templates</div>
        <div class="tech-item">HTML5</div>
        <div class="tech-item">CSS3</div>
        <div class="tech-item">JavaScript (ES6)</div>
        <div class="tech-item">RESTful API</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    

    <!-- Learning Outcomes -->
    <section class="about-section">
      <h2><svg class="section-icon" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="#icon-graduation" xlink:href="#icon-graduation"></use></svg> Learning Outcomes</h2>
      <p>After using this tool, you will be able to:</p>
      <ul class="outcomes-list">
        <li><svg class="check-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#icon-check" xlink:href="#icon-check"></use></svg> Convert binary numbers to decimal and hexadecimal</li>
        <li><svg class="check-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#icon-check" xlink:href="#icon-check"></use></svg> Explain how computers represent colors using binary</li>
        <li><svg class="check-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#icon-check" xlink:href="#icon-check"></use></svg> Identify the binary patterns for primary and secondary colors</li>
        <li><svg class="check-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#icon-check" xlink:href="#icon-check"></use></svg> Understand the 24-bit true color system (16.7 million colors)</li>
        <li><svg class="check-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#icon-check" xlink:href="#icon-check"></use></svg> Recognize the relationship between bit patterns and color intensity</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Credits -->
    <section class="about-section">
      <h2><svg class="section-icon" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="#icon-credits" xlink:href="#icon-credits"></use></svg> Credits</h2>
      <p>
        This project was developed as an educational tool for computer science
        students learning about binary number systems and digital color
        representation.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Project Type:</strong> Web-Based Educational Tool<br />
        <strong>License:</strong> MIT
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>

